+class PendingSpellAttack(_StrictModel):
+    """An attack-roll spell's attack roll that has NOT yet been resolved (#1270).
+
+    SRD: a spell with an attack roll (Guiding Bolt: "make a ranged spell attack")
+    spends its slot at cast time but requires a separate attack() call to resolve
+    the hit. The action economy gate tracks action_purpose='cast' to prevent
+    double-acting (cast + attack or cast + cast in one turn), BUT the spell's
+    attack roll IS PART OF THE CAST ACTION per SRD 5.2 — it shouldn't burn a
+    second action.
+
+    So cast_spell records a PENDING spell attack on the COMBAT (one per caster,
+    one per round) instead of stamping action_purpose='cast'; the next attack()
+    from that caster against the recorded target materializes the hit and clears
+    this record (allowing the attack to bypass the action-economy gate). A miss
+    or an attack on a different target bypasses both the spell check AND the action
+    gate, then clears this record so the action remains spent on something else.
+
+    ADDITIVE: `Combat.pending_spell_attack` defaults to `None`, so every existing
+    snapshot deserializes unchanged. Only attack-roll spells that set
+    automated=false ever create one."""
+
+    source_id: str  # the caster's character id (matched against attack()'s attacker)
+    target_ids: list[str]  # target ids for the attack (matched against attack()'s target); may be multiple for AoE
+    spell: str  # the spell's canonical name
+
+
